{"id": "EUVD-2026-81387", "enisaUuid": "05e3c4b1-827f-38ca-b0f9-405f1308513f", "description": "A flaw was found in flatpak-builder where Git hooks are not disabled when applying patch sources with use-git-am: true. An attacker who can provide a malicious source containing a Git post-applypatch hook can cause the hook to execute on the host during the build process, resulting in arbitrary code execution with the privileges of the user running flatpak-builder.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T07:27:33", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T11:21:31", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:80495", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:80496", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:80973", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:84832", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:84833", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:84834", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:84842", "https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:86714", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-86320", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2471023", "https://github.com/flatpak/flatpak-builder/security/advisories/GHSA-j5p8-jgjc-f3xv"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-86320", "GHSA-rvpr-5p35-6vf8"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "147e501a-8554-3f2e-9dd5-fe97f9cd33e3", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:1.2.3-1.el9_8.1"}, {"id": "3f21d17b-de60-3b82-a3b9-87e559ed6888", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10.0 Extended Update Support", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:1.4.4-1.el10_0.1"}, {"id": "59d95cba-51da-3092-a96b-850d403b96f2", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Enterprise Linux 9.2 Update Services for SAP Solutions", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0:1.2.2-2.el9_2"}, {"id": "5d4ac